radeon: cross-check TCL-bypass VAP_VTX_SIZE against VAP_OUT_VTX_FMT

DRAFT for review; not wired into the DKMS patch series.

A TCL-bypass draw whose VAP_VTX_SIZE (0x20B4) is smaller than the vertex
tuple advertised by VAP_OUT_VTX_FMT_0/1 (0x2090/0x2094) starves the GA:
it waits forever for tuple dwords the VAP never delivers, latches the
GA-busy RBBM signature, and stalls the ring globally.  The CS checker
passes such an IB today because 0x2090, 0x2094, and 0x2140
(VAP_CNTL_STATUS, which carries R300_VAP_TCL_BYPASS) sit in the
mkregtable safe lists, so r100_cs_parse_packet0 never routes them to
r300_packet0_check and no state is tracked; track->vtx_size feeds only
the buffer-coverage math in r100_cs_track_check.

Track VAP_OUT_VTX_FMT_0/1, VAP_CNTL_STATUS, and the
VAP_PROG_STREAM_CNTL_EXT swizzles by moving them out of the safe lists
into explicit r300_packet0_check cases.  At draw time (every
PACKET3_3D_DRAW_* case in r300_packet3_check) decode the output tuple's
dword requirement -- position 4, point size 1, colors 4 each, texture
coordinates their 3-bit component counts -- and reject with -EINVAL when
VAP_VTX_SIZE is strictly smaller.  The check runs only when the command
stream itself proves the configuration: TCL_BYPASS set by a
VAP_CNTL_STATUS write in this CS, both format words and VAP_VTX_SIZE
written in this CS, all eight VAP_PROG_STREAM_CNTL_EXT_0..7 written in
this CS with the identity swizzle (0xF688F688), and no undecoded format
bits.  Partial EXT coverage (fewer than eight identity writes) causes the
check to decline so stale PSC expansion in unwritten slots cannot
hide a VTX_SIZE under-feed.  Any other missing or ambiguous input also declines
(permissive default), because the PSC can legitimately expand a narrower
fetch and inherited state is invisible to the parser.

The radeon/reg_srcs/rs480 hunk applies on top of the series member that
creates that table (0021-rs480-cs-checker-r400-us-allowlist.patch); the
other hunks apply to the base radeon-unified-0.3 tree.  Regenerated
*_reg_safe.h tables follow automatically from the Makefile mkregtable
rule.

